          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mb-6">
            11. Common Mistakes to Avoid
          </h2>

          <div class="space-y-6 my-8">
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Trusting an old review on sweeteners</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                SEEQ's listings disagree on whether a given product uses sucralose, stevia, monk fruit or a mix. If you avoid any of them, a review from last year or a different flavor's listing is not good enough. Read the ingredient panel of the exact tub or packet you buy before you drink it.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Assuming viral means tested</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                A brand can sell millions of scoops through TikTok without ever submitting a batch to NSF, Informed Sport or Clean Label Project. SEEQ shows no such certification that we could find. If you are drug-tested or buying for pregnancy, choose a product whose certificate you can look up.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Comparing cost per scoop instead of per gram</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                A 22 g scoop and a 25 g scoop are not the same dose, and clear whey scoops are often smaller still. Divide price by servings, then by grams of protein, then multiply by 25. That number shows how much of SEEQ's price is protein and how much is format.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Mixing it like a regular shake</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                Clear whey needs plenty of cold water, 14 to 16 oz per scoop per SEEQ's directions, and a short rest to let the foam settle. Shaking it in a small amount of water, or adding milk, makes it taste harsh and foamy and wastes the reason you paid extra for it.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Buying from unknown Amazon resellers</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                Viral protein brands attract third-party sellers with old or questionable stock. On Amazon, check that the seller line shows the brand's own storefront, SEEQ Supply at the time of writing, and look at the best-by date when the tub arrives. If it looks tampered with, return it.
              </p>
